.TH MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CPP 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq_notify_cpp \- C++17 publisher library for the Mu2e DAQ notification server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <mu2edaq_notify/notify.hpp>
// In\-tree CMake: add_subdirectory(), then link mu2edaq::notify.
// Installed tree: find_package(CURL REQUIRED), then include
//   <prefix>/lib/cmake/mu2edaq_notify/mu2edaq_notify\-targets.cmake
// (no package Config file is installed, so find_package(mu2edaq_notify)
// does not work). Plain link line: \-lmu2edaq_notify \-lcurl

namespace mu2edaq::notify {
struct Options {
    std::string server_url;     // "" : $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_URL, then discovery
    std::string fallback_url;   // "" : $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_FALLBACK_URL, then
                                //      ANNOUNCE meta.fallback_url
    std::string token;          // "" : $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN
    std::string source = "cpp";
    std::string category;       // "" : $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CATEGORY
    std::string host;           // "" : gethostname()
    long timeout_ms = 5000;
    bool discover = true;
};
using Meta = std::map<std::string, std::string>;

class Publisher {
public:
    explicit Publisher(Options opts = {});
    bool publish(const std::string& severity, const std::string& title,
                 const std::string& message = "", const Meta& meta = {},
                 const std::string& category = "");
    bool debug(t, m = "", meta = {}, cat = "");    // also info, warning,
    bool error(t, m = "", meta = {}, cat = "");    // critical
    const std::string& server_url() const;
    const std::string& fallback_url() const;
};

struct DiscoveredServer { std::string primary, fallback; };
DiscoveredServer discover_server_pair(double timeout_s = 2.0);
std::string      discover_server(double timeout_s = 2.0);
}
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publishes one event per call to
.B POST /api/events
on
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1)
with libcurl. The JSON body carries
.BR severity ,
.BR title ,
.BR message ,
.BR source ,
.BR host ,
.B category
and
.BR meta ;
all values are strings.
.PP
.B Address resolution
is lazy: on the first
.BR publish ()
the publisher fills an empty
.B server_url
from
.B $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_URL
and an empty
.B fallback_url
from
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_FALLBACK_URL ,
then, if
.B discover
is true and either is still empty, sends one mu2edaq\-discovery DISCOVER
(multicast 239.255.42.99:28999, filter
.BR app=notify ,
2 s timeout) and takes the first matching ANNOUNCE. That first call can
therefore block for up to 2 s. Resolution happens once per object and is
never retried; if nothing answered, every later
.B publish()
returns false without sending. The client is self\-contained and does not
link the mu2edaq\-discovery library.
.PP
.B Delivery.
.B publish()
tries the primary, and the fallback only when libcurl reports a
transport\-level error (DNS, connect, timeout, TLS). Any HTTP reply ends the
attempt. It returns true on 2xx. It never throws, and it logs nothing: the
return value is the only signal. Severity is not validated here; the server
replaces an unknown severity with
.BR info .
TLS peer verification is libcurl's default (on).
.PP
.B Credentials.
The bearer token is sent to whichever address is used, including one taken
from an unauthenticated discovery reply. Set
.B server_url
explicitly where that matters.
.PP
.B Thread safety.
.B publish()
mutates the object on first use (lazy resolution) without a lock, and the
constructor calls
.BR curl_global_init (3),
which is not thread\-safe. Construct publishers before starting threads, and
give each thread its own publisher or call
.B publish()
once on the constructing thread first.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_URL
Primary server URL.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_FALLBACK_URL
Fallback server URL.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN
Publisher bearer token.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CATEGORY
Default category.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build and test the library (Linux, macOS, or Windows 11 with MSVC, where
.B ws2_32
is linked automatically):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cmake \-S . \-B build && cmake \-\-build build
ctest \-\-test\-dir build   # CppUnit tests; silently absent without CppUnit
.fi
.RE
.PP
Publish:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq::notify::Options o;
o.server_url = "https://mu2edaq\-pager.fnal.gov";
o.source = "dtc\-monitor";
o.category = "Trigger";
mu2edaq::notify::Publisher pub(o);
if (!pub.error("DTC link down", "ROC link 3 lost lock",
               {{"run", "107001"}}))
    std::cerr << "page not accepted\en";
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I src/cpp/examples/publish_example.cpp
is a complete program; CMake builds and installs it as
.BR publish_example .
